"Chicago is a big American city on Lake Michigan, at a glance much like the Chicago of Alan's Earth."
"Money is the US dollar, and phones, apps, rideshares and the internet work as on Alan's Earth."
"Earth has lived with the Artonan System since 1963, and Chicagoans take superhumans for granted."
"The System chooses a few teenagers as Avowed, superhumans who must register their powers."
"The city hires Avowed heroes-in-residence, whose fights and rescues fill the local news."
"Artonan Consulate 4, a grey concrete-and-glass cube behind a fence, is where the Avowed register."
"An alien called Gorgon sits chained at the consulate's front desk; tourists call him the Desk Demon."
"The consulate teaches classes in Artonan life, logograms and wordchaining to anyone who signs up."
"A wordchain is a prayer offering luck or peace of mind to an Opposite on another world."
"A House of Healing, with a healer and nurses trained in healing wordchains, treats power injuries."
"Some seven years ago a villain called Body Drainer killed twenty-seven people in the city."
"The L's elevated trains run through the city, and the Red Line runs all night."
"At the end of January it is deep winter, snowing, in the twenties Fahrenheit, colder off the lake."
"Shelters, hospitals, police and social services work as in any American city."
